In article <1993Jan5.090738.7430@siemens.co.at> Wolfgang Howdii Howurek writes:

>Now, what I could find out: monsters will not only hit you, they
>will hit also other monsters. Perhaps there are more specific
>details in the use of a ring of conflict, but I'm not the guru of hack.

That's basically what it does.  If you're wearing a ring of conflict,
monsters will hit each other instead of hitting you.  The only way
you'll get hit is if you're standing next to a monster that isn't next
to any other monsters that it can hit instead of you.

I think the ring of conflict is probably the most powerful item in the
game, aside from the wand of wishing and maybe the wand of polymorph.
It lets you escape all those nasty multiple-monster situations that
can kill weak characters, and makes it much easier to deal with
beehives, throne rooms, etc.  If you want to set up a fairly easy game
of nethack, keep generating Wizards until you get one with a ring of
conflict and decent stats.  The ring plus the athame make a Wizard
very hard to kill.

